  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 257 AM EDT Wed Aug 26 2026\n\n=====  Drier Weather Returns Friday and into the Weekend =====\n\nWe'll be in a post-frontal environment by Friday morning, so we can \nexpect dry weather to take over for the end of the week and into the \nweekend. There could be one last lingering shower chance near Lake \nCumberland early in the morning, but otherwise we will see \ndecreasing clouds. A secondary moisture-starved cold front looks to \nsweep south through the area sometime during Friday, but little to \nno change will be felt. Highs on Friday are expected to be in the \nmid to upper 80s. \n\nUpper ridging will continue to build eastward over the weekend, with \nsfc high pressure spread out across the Ohio Valley. Dry and sunny \nweather is expected, with temps creeping up to near 90F over the \nweekend as the ridge builds. \n\n===== Potential For Temps in the 90s Next Week =====\n\nThe upper ridge will become a bit more suppressed by next week as an \nupper low pivots across the US/Canadian border. However, sfc high \npressure will remain just to our east, placing our area deep within \nthe warmer return flow. Ensemble guidance suggests we'll see temps \nclimb well into the 90s next week, with the NBM topping out in the \nmid-90s next week. However, confidence in this remains somewhat low \ngiven the warm bias of the NBM. However, despite this potential for \ntemps in the 90s, sfc dewpoints mainly in the 60s could yield heat \nindices mainly below 100. Additionally, the 100-member Grand \nEnsemble is not too impressed with heat indices next week, with just \na 25% chance or less for heat index values over 100F. Will be worth \nwatching over the coming days, but we could see these high temp \nforecast for next week decrease slightly as we get into better model \nresolution.",
